\newlabel{tab:strictfreeze}{{10}{22}{The strict-freeze control (condition~H) beside condition~D on sixteen cells: the six that met the degradation definition under the superseded trend baseline, plus ILI, plus the five gate-passing survivors of \S \ref {sec:forecasting:results}, plus all four Moirai/ETTm2 value-cells. \textbf {B$-$H keeps B$-$D's sign on twelve and reverses it on all four ETTm2 cells}, where condition~D's margin was the input projection re-fitting rather than the encoder being held still. B$-$D is restricted to the seeds condition~H ran, and a cell with fewer than three H seeds is excluded and named by the emitter rather than printed thin. $n$ is shown on every row and is not constant down the column; ILI's $452$ is its whole training split rather than a cap (Table~\ref {tab:heldout_all}). Generated by \texttt {scripts/cell\_matrix.py --latex}}{table.caption.17}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {11}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Condition E (LoRA, $r{=}8$, $\alpha {=}16$) on the eight Moirai value-cells that lacked it.} All contrasts are held-out test MSE, normalised by the cell's zero-shot test MSE, in percentage points; $\pm $ is SEM over the seeds in the Seeds column. Sign convention matches B$-$D and B$-$H throughout: \textbf  {positive means full fine-tuning did worse than the comparison arm}. B$-$D is recomputed on E's seeds, so it is comparable to B$-$E within a row and may differ from the same cell's row in Table~\ref {tab:heldout_all}, which averages that cell's full seed set. Parenthesised counts are the seeds sharing the mean's sign. $\ell _2$ weight drift is exactly $0.0$ for every run and is not shown: LoRA leaves the base parameters untouched by construction, which is why CKA, not drift, is the representation measure here. Rows ordered by D$-$E.}}{23}{table.caption.18}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:lora_valuecells}{{11}{23}{\textbf {Condition E (LoRA, $r{=}8$, $\alpha {=}16$) on the eight Moirai value-cells that lacked it.} All contrasts are held-out test MSE, normalised by the cell's zero-shot test MSE, in percentage points; $\pm $ is SEM over the seeds in the Seeds column. Sign convention matches B$-$D and B$-$H throughout: \textbf {positive means full fine-tuning did worse than the comparison arm}. B$-$D is recomputed on E's seeds, so it is comparable to B$-$E within a row and may differ from the same cell's row in Table~\ref {tab:heldout_all}, which averages that cell's full seed set. Parenthesised counts are the seeds sharing the mean's sign. $\ell _2$ weight drift is exactly $0.0$ for every run and is not shown: LoRA leaves the base parameters untouched by construction, which is why CKA, not drift, is the representation measure here. Rows ordered by D$-$E}{table.caption.18}{}}
